## 53. Chinese Coding Example

Given:

```text
"sun rises east" = ka po mi
"sun sets west"  = ka tu na
"moon rises west" = lo po na
```

Compare first two:

Common:

```text
sun
```

Common code:

```text
ka
```

Therefore:

```text
sun = ka
```

Compare first and third:

Common:

```text
rises
```

Common code:

```text
po
```

Therefore:

```text
rises = po
```

Compare second and third:

Common:

```text
west
```

Common code:

```text
na
```

Therefore:

```text
west = na
```

Remaining:

```text
east = mi
sets = tu
moon = lo
```

---

## 54. Mixed Coding

A code may contain multiple components.

Example:

```text
CAT → C3A1T20
```

Here:

```text
letter + position
```

Another:

```text
CAT → 3-1-20
```

The separator is irrelevant unless the question says otherwise.

---

## 55. Letter + Number Coding

Example:

```text
DOG
D = 4
O = 15
G = 7
```

Possible code:

```text
D4 O15 G7
```

or:

```text
4157
```

Always inspect the examples.

---

## 56. Symbol Coding

Suppose:

```text
A = @
B = #
C = $
D = %
```

Then:

```text
BAD → #@%
```

This is direct substitution.

---

## 57. Operation Symbol Coding

Sometimes symbols represent mathematical operations.

Example:

```text
+ means ×
− means ÷
× means +
÷ means −
```

Then:

```text
8 + 2
```

actually means:

```text
8 × 2 = 16
```

The important rule:

> Decode the operators first, then calculate.

---

## 58. Operator Coding Example

Given:

```text
+ = −
− = ×
× = ÷
÷ = +
```

Question:

```text
12 + 3 × 2
```

Decode:

```text
12 − 3 ÷ 2
```

Then apply normal mathematical precedence:

```text
3 ÷ 2 = 1.5
12 − 1.5 = 10.5
```

---

## 59. Conditional Coding

A code can depend on conditions.

Example:

```text
If first letter is a vowel → +2
If first letter is a consonant → −1
```

Then:

```text
APPLE
```

starts with A:

```text
A + 2 = C
```

while:

```text
BALL
```

starts with B:

```text
B − 1 = A
```

---

## 60. Conditional Flowchart

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Input word] --> B{Condition}
    B -->|Vowel first| C[Rule A]
    B -->|Consonant first| D[Rule B]
    C --> E[Final code]
    D --> E
```

---
